    "chunk_text": "(I) The following Persons are entitled to be appointed to the Panel of a particular Special Mediation Board Area whose names may be so submitted for appointment.\n\n(a) A person eligible to be appointed as a Member of the Panel of Mediators in respect of the Special Mediation Boards shall be between 35 to 70 years of age and;\n\n(b) has any professional qualification obtained from a recognized professional body established by or under any written law;\n\n(c) has been or is public officer.\n\n(I) (A) The following Individuals are entitled to submit nominations other than themselves for appointment to the Panel of a particular Special Mediation Board area:\n\n(i) A Public Officer or a Provincial Public Officer serving as the Head of a Department or as the Regional Head of a Department in an office located within the Administrative District at which that particular Special Mediation Board area is situated:\n\n(ii) A Head of a Place or religious worship or of school situated in that particular Special Mediation Board area;\n\n(iii) A retired Head of a Department or School principal residing in that particular Special Mediation Board area; (B) Any board, Organizations or Institution which has been in existence at least for a period of five years and which is engaged in carrying out or doing anyone or more of the under mentioned objectives;\n\n(i) The enhancement of educational, religious, moral or spiritual, advancement of the community\n\n(ii) The enhancement of social welfare and eradication of poverty\n\n(iii) The enhancement of rural or community development.\n\n(iv) The enhancement of culture of sports\n\n(v) The enhancement of projects, programmes and activities intending providing and supplying basic needs of the peoples such as health, food and shelter etc. (C) The following District Secretaries/Divisional Secretaries are entitled to submit nominations for appointment to the Panel of a particular Special Mediation Board Area:-"
